/-!
# The covariant towers of the Standard Model

The thirteen covariant towers of the Standard Model in the notation of the classification of
invariants, their commutation across sectors, and the algebra they generate.

## i. Overview

The covariant fields of the Standard Model, and every polynomial expression in them, live in
the covariant field algebra of the Standard Model `StandardModel.fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra`,
which carries the global gauge action, the Lorentz action and the mass-weight grading. This file
names its thirteen covariant towers in the notation of the classification of invariants, records
that towers of different sectors commute, and defines the field algebra they generate.

The thirteen towers are the field strength, the Higgs field and its conjugate, and the five
fermion species in three generations with their conjugates, each with all of its covariant
derivatives. Section A names them. Section B records the symmetry of the field-strength tower
at a dual vector vanishing on brackets. Section C states the commutation of towers of
different sectors, which is what the classification of invariants is written in terms of, and
section D defines the field algebra.

## ii. Key results

- `LocalCovFieldAlgebra.covF`, `LocalCovFieldAlgebra.covH` and their companions : the thirteen
  covariant towers.
- `LocalCovFieldAlgebra.F_comm_H` and its companions : the towers of different sectors
  commute.
- `LocalCovFieldAlgebra.fieldAlgebra` : the algebra generated by all the covariant towers.

## iii. Table of contents

- A. The covariant fields of the Standard Model
- B. The field strength at a dual vector vanishing on brackets
- C. The cross-sector commutation rules
- D. The field algebra

## iv. References

* None.

-/

@[expose] public section

namespace StandardModel

open TensorProduct Matrix MatrixGroups Lorentz

namespace LocalCovFieldAlgebra

/-!

## A. The covariant fields of the Standard Model

The thirteen covariant towers the theory is written in are the towers of the covariant field
algebra of the Standard Model. The field-strength tower is real-linear in its value index.

-/

/-- The covariant derivatives `∇_l F_{μν}` of the field strength inside the covariant field
  algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covF {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) (μ ν : Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3) :
    Module.Dual ℝ GaugeAlgebra →ₗ[ℝ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  gaugeFieldStrength l μ ν

/-- The covariant derivatives `∇_l H` of the Higgs field inside the covariant field algebra of the
  Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covH {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ HiggsVec →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  higgsField l

/-- The covariant derivatives `∇_l H̄` of the conjugate Higgs field inside the covariant field
  algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covBarH {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ (ConjModule HiggsVec) →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  conjHiggsField l

/-- The covariant derivatives of the `i`-th generation down-type quark singlet inside the
  covariant field algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covD (i : Fin 3) {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ DownSinglet →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  downSingletField i l

/-- The covariant derivatives of the `i`-th generation conjugate down-type quark singlet inside
  the covariant field algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covBarD (i : Fin 3) {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ (ConjModule DownSinglet) →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  conjDownSingletField i l

/-- The covariant derivatives of the `i`-th generation up-type quark singlet inside the covariant
  field algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covU (i : Fin 3) {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ UpSinglet →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  upSingletField i l

/-- The covariant derivatives of the `i`-th generation conjugate up-type quark singlet inside the
  covariant field algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covBarU (i : Fin 3) {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ (ConjModule UpSinglet) →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  conjUpSingletField i l

/-- The covariant derivatives of the `i`-th generation quark doublet inside the covariant field
  algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covQ (i : Fin 3) {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ QuarkDoublet →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  quarkDoubletField i l

/-- The covariant derivatives of the `i`-th generation conjugate quark doublet inside the
  covariant field algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covBarQ (i : Fin 3) {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ (ConjModule QuarkDoublet) →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  conjQuarkDoubletField i l

/-- The covariant derivatives of the `i`-th generation lepton doublet inside the covariant field
  algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covL (i : Fin 3) {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ LeptonDoubletV →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  leptonDoubletField i l

/-- The covariant derivatives of the `i`-th generation conjugate lepton doublet inside the
  covariant field algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covBarL (i : Fin 3) {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ (ConjModule LeptonDoubletV) →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  conjLeptonDoubletField i l

/-- The covariant derivatives of the `i`-th generation charged-lepton singlet inside the covariant
  field algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covE (i : Fin 3) {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ LeptonSinglet →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  leptonSingletField i l

/-- The covariant derivatives of the `i`-th generation conjugate charged-lepton singlet inside the
  covariant field algebra of the Standard Model. -/
noncomputable abbrev covBarE (i : Fin 3) {n : ℕ} (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) :
    Module.Dual ℂ (ConjModule LeptonSinglet) →ₗ[ℂ] fieldData.LocalCovFieldAlgebra :=
  conjLeptonSingletField i l

/-!

## B. The field strength at a dual vector vanishing on brackets

-/

/-- At a dual vector vanishing on every bracket, such as the hypercharge coordinate, the
  field-strength tower is symmetric in its derivative slots, at every order. In the covariant field
  algebra of the Standard Model those covariant derivatives are ordinary ones. The components along
  the non-abelian factors have no such symmetry. -/
lemma covF_comp_perm_of_map_lie {φ : Module.Dual ℝ GaugeAlgebra}
    (hφ : ∀ x y : GaugeAlgebra, φ ⁅x, y⁆ = 0) {n : ℕ} (σ : Equiv.Perm (Fin n))
    (l : Fin n → (Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)) (μ ν : Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3) :
    covF (l ∘ σ) μ ν φ = covF l μ ν φ :=
  Subtype.ext (fieldData.covDerivFieldStrength_eq_of_perm_of_map_lie
    (φ := gaugeDualToLie φ) (fun x y => by
      obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := gaugeAlgebraEquiv.surjective x
      obtain ⟨b, rfl⟩ := gaugeAlgebraEquiv.surjective y
      have e : ⁅gaugeAlgebraEquiv a, gaugeAlgebraEquiv b⁆ = gaugeAlgebraEquiv ⁅a, b⁆ :=
        (gaugeAlgebraEquiv.map_lie a b).symm
      have : gaugeAlgebraEquiv.symm ⁅gaugeAlgebraEquiv a, gaugeAlgebraEquiv b⁆ = ⁅a, b⁆ := by
        rw [e]; exact LieEquiv.symm_apply_apply _ _
      exact (congrArg φ this).trans (hφ a b)) (σ.ofFn_comp_perm l) μ ν)

/-!

## C. The cross-sector commutation rules

A bosonic tower is central (`fieldStrength_commute`, `higgsField_commute`,
`conjHiggsField_commute`), so it commutes with every tower of another sector. The rules are
named as the classification of invariants uses them.

-/

/-- A field-strength tower commutes with a Higgs tower. -/
lemma F_comm_H {n m : ℕ} (l : Fin n → Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3) (μ ν : Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)
    (ψ : Module.Dual ℝ GaugeAlgebra) (l' : Fin m → Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)
    (φ : Module.Dual ℂ HiggsVec) :
    Commute (covF l μ ν ψ) (covH l' φ) :=
  fieldStrength_commute l μ ν (gaugeDualToLie ψ) _

/-- A field-strength tower commutes with a conjugate Higgs tower. -/
lemma F_comm_barH {n m : ℕ} (l : Fin n → Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3) (μ ν : Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)
    (ψ : Module.Dual ℝ GaugeAlgebra) (l' : Fin m → Fin 1 ⊕ Fin 3)
    (φ : Module.Dual ℂ (ConjModule HiggsVec)) :
    Commute (covF l μ ν ψ) (covBarH l' φ) :=
  fieldStrength_commute l μ ν (gaugeDualToLie ψ) _

/-- A field-strength tower commutes with a down-type quark singlet tower. -/
